    "translations": {
      "en": {
        "description": "A weak champion that is difficult to pilot, truly testing the player's patience and endurance.\\nGnar's playstyle mainly revolves around pinging the enemy Nexus to build up stats and stacks every round.\\nHis starting deck offers multiple ways to damage the Nexus, but the units themselves are generally too weak and lack meaningful synergy with one another.\\n[p:P0166|The Beast Within] generates a Stun card for defense, but it is simply not enough for a mana-starved champion like Gnar.\\n[cd:05BC166|Pokey Stick] is a highly versatile and effective card that can be used in many situations within this deck.\\nTo pilot this champion optimally, you need to deal damage to the enemy Nexus with your units during attacking rounds. On defensive rounds, use [cd:05FR006|Tusk Speaker] or damage spells to safely build up your stats. Prioritize using your Stun card defensively, or to protect your units when going in for a massive attack with your built-up stats.\\nGnar is heavily dependent on the Powers and Items you draft during the adventure. You should prioritize [p:P0111|Sorcery], [p:P0113|Spellslinger], or defensive Powers to slowly scale up your units over time. Strong item pickups for Gnar include [i:I0118|Power Chord] and [i:I0012|Shadow Totem].\\nThis champion is only suited for lower-difficulty content, specifically adventures at 4-Stars and below.\\nGood luck if you actually plan on playing this champion!",
        "descriptionRaw": "A weak champion that is difficult to pilot, truly testing the player's patience and endurance.\\nGnar's playstyle mainly revolves around pinging the enemy Nexus to build up stats and stacks every round.\\nHis starting deck offers multiple ways to damage the Nexus, but the units themselves are generally too weak and lack meaningful synergy with one another.\\nThe Beast Within generates a Stun card for defense, but it is simply not enough for a mana-starved champion like Gnar.\\nPokey Stick is a highly versatile and effective card that can be used in many situations within this deck.\\nTo pilot this champion optimally, you need to deal damage to the enemy Nexus with your units during attacking rounds. On defensive rounds, use Tusk Speaker or damage spells to safely build up your stats. Prioritize using your Stun card defensively, or to protect your units when going in for a massive attack with your built-up stats.\\nGnar is heavily dependent on the Powers and Items you draft during the adventure. You should prioritize Sorcery, Spellslinger, or defensive Powers to slowly scale up your units over time. Strong item pickups for Gnar include Power Chord and Shadow Totem.\\nThis champion is only suited for lower-difficulty content, specifically adventures at 4-Stars and below.\\nGood luck if you actually plan on playing this champion!",
        "name": "Gnar",
        "optimalStars": "3 Stars ",
        "playStyle": "Controll // Aggro",
        "regions": [
          "BandleCity",
          "Freljord"
        ],
        "tags": [
          "Impacts",
          "L champion"
        ],
        "tier": "C tier"
      }
    }
