    "translations": {
      "en": {
        "description": "Strong offense, weak defense, great sustain, completely reliant on the champion, easy to play, and fast adventure clears.\\n[cd:06SI012|Gwen] is an aggressive champion built for fast wins through explosive burst damage and massive Nexus healing via the [k:Hallowed|Hallowed] mechanic.\\nHer main strength is inheriting power from fallen Hallowed allies, turning that attack into direct Nexus damage and triggering her Snip Snip! skill to heal your Nexus to full.\\nAt 2 stars, Threading the Needle copies Hallowed buffs onto the unit attacking in the 2nd slot from the left. Because of this, you must position Gwen in the 2nd slot from the left to double-dip Hallowed buffs and level her up on her very first attack.\\nAt 6 stars, Last Dance summons 4 [cd:06SI009|Strike Up the Band] units at game start and grants an immediate Rally, allowing you to flood the board and hit peak Hallowed stacks right on round 1.\\nThe primary game plan is using cheap units like [cd:06SI016|Boisterous Host] and [cd:06SI028|Phantom Butler] to block and build Hallowed stacks -> summoning Gwen when you have the attack token -> placing Gwen in the 2nd slot from the left to double-dip Hallowed and level up to close the game.\\nIt is recommended to draft powers that boost spell and skill damage or mana powers to deploy Gwen early. If you haven't unlocked 4 stars yet, prioritize drafting Overwhelm to prevent enemies from chump-blocking your attacks.",
        "descriptionRaw": "Strong offense, weak defense, great sustain, completely reliant on the champion, easy to play, and fast adventure clears.\\nGwen is an aggressive champion built for fast wins through explosive burst damage and massive Nexus healing via the Hallowed mechanic.\\nHer main strength is inheriting power from fallen Hallowed allies, turning that attack into direct Nexus damage and triggering her Snip Snip! skill to heal your Nexus to full.\\nAt 2 stars, Threading the Needle copies Hallowed buffs onto the unit attacking in the 2nd slot from the left. Because of this, you must position Gwen in the 2nd slot from the left to double-dip Hallowed buffs and level her up on her very first attack.\\nAt 6 stars, Last Dance summons 4 Strike Up the Band units at game start and grants an immediate Rally, allowing you to flood the board and hit peak Hallowed stacks right on round 1.\\nThe primary game plan is using cheap units like Boisterous Host and Phantom Butler to block and build Hallowed stacks -> summoning Gwen when you have the attack token -> placing Gwen in the 2nd slot from the left to double-dip Hallowed and level up to close the game.\\nIt is recommended to draft powers that boost spell and skill damage or mana powers to deploy Gwen early. If you haven't unlocked 4 stars yet, prioritize drafting Overwhelm to prevent enemies from chump-blocking your attacks.",
        "name": "Gwen",
        "optimalStars": "4 - 5 Stars",
        "playStyle": "Burn // Aggro",
        "regions": [
          "ShadowIsles"
        ],
        "tags": [
          "Aggro",
          "Healing",
          "Hallowed",
          "Solo Carry",
          "Glass cannon"
        ],
        "tier": "A+ Tier // Glass cannon with high sustain"
      }
    }
