    "translations": {
      "en": {
        "description": "A purely RNG-dependent champion that is easy to play and learn; your power level relies entirely on your luck.\\n\\n[cd:01PZ056|Heimerdinger] features a board control and swarm playstyle using Tech units, with infinite late-game scaling potential.\\n\\nHeimerdinger's core strength lies in his ability to convert every spell cast into a corresponding Turret in hand, while your Tech units gain stat and keyword buffs whenever you spend 6 or more spell mana.\\n\\nAt his 2-Star (C2) power, [p:P0629|Progress Pursued], you gain +1 starting mana and refill 1 spell mana whenever you summon a unit. This creates an operational loop: cast a spell -> create a unit -> play the unit -> refill spell mana.\\n\\nReaching his 3-Star (C3) power, [p:P0441|SCIENCE!!! II], spending 6 spell mana grants all Tech units in your hand and on the board even stronger random buffs from the upgrade pool.\\n\\nMost notably, with his 6-Star (C6) power, [p:P0535|Eureka!], all Tech allies in hand and on the board are granted 3 random upgrades right at the start of the game, while automatically summoning a [cd:01PZ056T1|Mk0: Wrenchbot] to establish board control on Round 1.\\n\\nThe primary strategy for this champion is to use cheap spells like [cd:07PZ015|Epic Scraptraption] to trigger spell casts whenever needed, then play 6-cost spells combined with [r:R0048|Chemtech Duplicator] to duplicate the spells. This double-triggers the upgrades for your Turret swarm to overwhelm the opponent and finish the game.\\n\\nAs a tip, you should prioritize Powers that refill spell mana each round, reduce spell costs, or grant team-wide Overwhelm to help your Tech board easily close out the match.",
        "descriptionRaw": "A purely RNG-dependent champion that is easy to play and learn; your power level relies entirely on your luck.\\n\\nHeimerdinger features a board control and swarm playstyle using Tech units, with infinite late-game scaling potential.\\n\\nHeimerdinger's core strength lies in his ability to convert every spell cast into a corresponding Turret in hand, while your Tech units gain stat and keyword buffs whenever you spend 6 or more spell mana.\\n\\nAt his 2-Star (C2) power, Progress Pursued, you gain +1 starting mana and refill 1 spell mana whenever you summon a unit. This creates an operational loop: cast a spell -> create a unit -> play the unit -> refill spell mana.\\n\\nReaching his 3-Star (C3) power, SCIENCE!!! II, spending 6 spell mana grants all Tech units in your hand and on the board even stronger random buffs from the upgrade pool.\\n\\nMost notably, with his 6-Star (C6) power, Eureka!, all Tech allies in hand and on the board are granted 3 random upgrades right at the start of the game, while automatically summoning a Mk0: Wrenchbot to establish board control on Round 1.\\n\\nThe primary strategy for this champion is to use cheap spells like Epic Scraptraption to trigger spell casts whenever needed, then play 6-cost spells combined with Chemtech Duplicator to duplicate the spells. This double-triggers the upgrades for your Turret swarm to overwhelm the opponent and finish the game.\\n\\nAs a tip, you should prioritize Powers that refill spell mana each round, reduce spell costs, or grant team-wide Overwhelm to help your Tech board easily close out the match.",
        "name": "Heimerdinger",
        "optimalStars": "4 Stars",
        "playStyle": "Control // Tech Swarm",
        "ratings": {
          "playstyleNote": ""
        },
        "regions": [
          "BandleCity",
          "PiltoverZaun"
        ],
        "tags": [
          "Control",
          "Spells",
          "Tech",
          "Creation",
          "Infinite Value"
        ],
        "tier": "B Tier // Infinite Gacha"
      }
    }
  },
