    "translations": {
      "en": {
        "description": "[cd:01IO015|Yasuo] is the hallmark of absolute board control in The Path of Champions. The strength of [cd:01IO015|Yasuo] comes from stunning the opponent's strongest unit via 3 Stars alongside control stun spells that lock down the battlefield.\\nAt 3 Stars with [p:P0036|Way of the Wind II], you automatically stun the Strongest enemy at Round Start, neutralizing dangerous opposing units before they can act. Reaching 6 Stars with [p:P0473|Tempest|icon], all stunned enemies are automatically recalled to hand at Round End.\\nYour primary early-game carry is [cd:01IO008|Fae Bladetwirler], which continuously gains +2|+0 whenever an enemy is stunned or recalled. Combined with flexible crowd control spells like [cd:01IO046|Steel Tempest] and [cd:02IO005|Concussive Palm], you completely dictate the pace of the game and keep [cd:01IO015|Yasuo] safe before every skirmish.\\nFor adventure powers, prioritize spell support powers like [p:P0111|Sorcery] or [p:P0113|Spellslinger] to defend and attack with greater flexibility. If you find [p:P0064|Hold It!], it doubles the amount of stunned enemies at Round Start, helping [cd:01IO015|Yasuo] level up at lightning speed and wipe the board clean in a single strike.",
        "descriptionRaw": "Yasuo is the hallmark of absolute board control in The Path of Champions. The strength of Yasuo comes from stunning the opponent's strongest unit via 3 Stars alongside control stun spells that lock down the battlefield.\\nAt 3 Stars with Way of the Wind II, you automatically stun the Strongest enemy at Round Start, neutralizing dangerous opposing units before they can act. Reaching 6 Stars with Tempest, all stunned enemies are automatically recalled to hand at Round End.\\nYour primary early-game carry is Fae Bladetwirler, which continuously gains +2|+0 whenever an enemy is stunned or recalled. Combined with flexible crowd control spells like Steel Tempest and Concussive Palm, you completely dictate the pace of the game and keep Yasuo safe before every skirmish.\\nFor adventure powers, prioritize spell support powers like Sorcery or Spellslinger to defend and attack with greater flexibility. If you find Hold It!, it doubles the amount of stunned enemies at Round Start, helping Yasuo level up at lightning speed and wipe the board clean in a single strike.",
        "name": "Yasuo",
        "optimalStars": "3 Stars",
        "playStyle": "Control // Stun Lockdown",
        "ratings": {
          "playstyleNote": "Dominant board control playstyle based on automatic Round Start stuns and clearing the board through Yasuo's passive strikes."
        },
        "regions": [
          "Ionia"
        ],
        "tags": [
          "Control",
          "Stun",
          "Recall",
          "Single Target",
          "Counter"
        ],
        "tier": "S Tier // Absolute lockdown and stun board wipe"
      }
    }
  },
